# What one machine costs an MCU image, in bytes, and how far it may drift.
#
# Read by `scripts/gates/nostd-mcu.sh`. Every figure here is MEASURED, on
# `thumbv7em-none-eabihf` with the toolchain named in MEASURED_WITH, from the
# staticlib `backends/rust/probes/nostd-footprint` produces — summing the
# `.text` sizes of every symbol `nm -C` reports whose name contains
# MACHINE_SYMBOLS.
#
# WHY A BUDGET AND NOT A TREND. A downstream bare-metal consumer measured this
# growing 60-198 bytes per instantiation across two SCE pins and filed it
# (2026-08-21) because nothing on our side could see it: the MCU gate compiled
# but linked nothing, so no gate in this repository had ever weighed a section.
# A budget is what turns "the engine got bigger" from a consumer's bug report
# into our own red.
#
# RE-PINNING IS A DECISION, NOT A CHORE. When a change legitimately grows what
# a machine costs, move TOTAL_BYTES and say in the commit message what the
# bytes bought. The gate fails on a DROP as well, which is not pedantry: the
# first shape of this probe emitted LLVM bitcode instead of machine code and
# `nm` reported zero symbols, so a one-sided gate would have passed forever on
# an empty measurement. A number that falls without a reason means the
# instrument stopped seeing, and that is the failure this file exists to
# prevent.

# Which symbols are the machine's: every one whose demangled name carries the
# probe machine's crate. That is the runtime's generic code monomorphised for
# it — `Engine<P>`, the `EngineHost<P>` adapter, Appendix D's transcription in
# `helpers::microstep` instantiated over that adapter, the event queue over its
# event type — and the policy generated for it. It is what an image pays AGAIN
# for every machine it holds, which is the number a consumer multiplies by
# their machine count. Code the runtime carries once per image whatever it
# holds (`is_error_event`, the string helpers) is not in it.
#
# WHY NOT `Engine<..>` ALONE, which is what this file weighed until the Rust
# backend moved onto Appendix D (2026-09-24). Where the microstep's code lives
# — the runtime or the template — is a choice this repository makes and
# remakes, and an instrument that weighs one side reads a MOVE as a change.
# That move, measured on both sides of it with one toolchain:
#
#                      Engine<..>   per machine   (diagnostics on)
#   before (fb30b83e)     1702          5858
#   after                 2318          4976
#
# `Engine<..>` alone would have called a 15% shrink a 36% growth. It had also
# never seen most of what a machine cost: 4156 of those 5858 bytes were in no
# symbol it weighed, among them the microstep itself, generated into every
# policy as `execute_microstep`, `try_transition_in_state`,
# `remove_conflicting_transitions` and `compute_exit_set` (1812 bytes).
#
# ⚠ The pattern relies on the v0 symbol-mangling scheme, which the toolchain
# above emits by default: a v0 name carries its concrete generic arguments, so
# `enter_states::<EngineHost<ParallelHistoryProbePolicy>>` names the machine.
# Under the legacy scheme it does not, and the set collapses — measured with
# `-C symbol-mangling-version=legacy` on the same tree: 3 symbols and 100
# bytes, against 36 and 4976. MIN_SYMBOLS is what makes that a red rather than
# a smaller number. It is a literal substring, not a regular expression.
MACHINE_SYMBOLS='sce_nostd_build_probe::'

# The toolchain the figures below were measured with. Not enforced: the lane
# installs whatever `stable` is on the day, and a toolchain that inlines
# differently moves these bytes with no change of ours. The gate prints this
# beside `rustc --version` when it fails, so a red that is only the toolchain
# says so, and a re-pin names the toolchain it was taken on.
MEASURED_WITH='rustc 1.98.1 (48a229cea 2026-09-01)'

# Sum of every machine symbol in the staticlib, as the engine ships.
TOTAL_BYTES=4976

# The same sum with `no_macrostep_diagnostics`, which compiles the macrostep
# REPORT out and leaves the bound in place.
#
# The difference — 24 bytes per machine — is the number that feature is worth,
# and it is here rather than in a commit message because it is the answer to a
# question a consumer asked: whether gating the diagnostics would recover what
# two commits cost their image. Measuring both ways is also what keeps the
# opt-out configuration from rotting — a feature nothing builds is a feature
# that stops compiling and nobody learns until a consumer sets it.
#
# It was 44 when the feature was offered and 48 just before the microstep moved
# into the runtime. The two places that refuse a macrostep now share one
# `refuse_macrostep`, which holds the report's only log call; before, each
# carried its own.
#
# WHAT THE REPORT WAS A FRACTION OF, measured at four pins in this same tree at
# one fixed path (`7f94b580` -> `7db6aebc` -> `e0fdd46b` -> `a8026fd6`), as
# `Engine<..>` sums — the metric of the time, not comparable with the figures
# above:
#
#   1072 -> 1418 -> 1418 -> 1666 bytes, i.e. +594 per instantiation over the
#   two commits that landed the macrostep ceiling (37a47335a3, e00d4eee04).
#
# So the report was 44 of 594 — **7%** — and the other 550 is the bound: the
# per-microstep budget and the guard that stops a refused chain being handed a
# second one. There is no version of this engine that both terminates and does
# not pay that. The figure is on `thumbv7em-none-eabihf` at `opt-level = "z"`;
# a consumer on another target or profile should expect the RATIO to hold and
# the absolutes not to.
#
# The report's `sce_log_error!` calls are inside the feature gate as well, and
# measured zero when there were two of them (2026-08-21): the sum was
# identical with and without them, because the format arguments live in
# `.rodata` and the call is a handful of instructions the linker folds
# elsewhere. A downstream consumer reached the same conclusion from the other
# end — with `lto = true` and no logger installed, their image had already
# discarded every `log::` call before we asked them to try.
TOTAL_BYTES_NO_DIAGNOSTICS=4952

# Drift allowed either way before the gate speaks, in BYTES. Wide enough that
# an unrelated inlining decision does not cry wolf, tight enough that one more
# copy of a cold path (the 2026-08-21 report's ~170 B per instantiation) does.
#
# It was 8 PERCENT while this file weighed `Engine<..>` alone: ±133 bytes of
# the 1666 it held then. What it encodes is a byte count, and a percentage of a
# figure that tripled would have let the cold path through (8% of 4976 is
# ±398). So the band is that one, carried over in bytes.
TOLERANCE_BYTES=133

# The instrument's own floor. Below this the probe is not measuring the machine
# at all — a renamed crate, a bitcode staticlib, a driver that stopped driving,
# a toolchain that mangles without generic arguments — and every byte figure
# above it is meaningless. The set held 36 symbols at the last re-pin and 35
# before it, across a change that moved half its bytes between the runtime and
# the policy; the legacy scheme leaves 3, and the bitcode staticlib left none.
# The floor sits between, with room for a refactor to move the count by a
# dozen.
MIN_SYMBOLS=24
